      "value": "Dalakas criteria for SPS: (1) Stiffness in the axial muscles, particularly abdominal and thoracolumbar paraspinal muscles, leading to a fixed deformity: hyperlordosis. (2) Superimposed painful spasms precipitated by unexpected noises, emotional stress, or tactile stimuli. (3) Confirmation by electromyography (EMG). (4) Absence of neurological or cognitive impairment that could explain the stiffness. (5) Positive serology: GAD or amphiphysin autoantibodies. (6) Response to diazepam.",
